;; TON PRIMES — Bounty vault message schemas (concept §3.3).
;; Opcodes: /shared/opcodes.ts `BOUNTY_VAULT`.
;; Era bounties and special-number rebates are paid on the ledger's word;
;; program bounties (quests) come from contracts allow-listed by address at
;; genesis — the allow-list is a genesis-time constant, not a post-deploy
;; admin knob.

;; ---- genesis-only bootstrap ----

set_wallet#90000003
    query_id:uint64
    jetton_wallet_addr:MsgAddress
  = InternalMsgBody;
;; The vault's own PRIMES jetton wallet. Sender MUST equal the genesis-script
;; address (100); one-shot (104). Same shape as stake.tlb's `set_wallet`.

;; ---- inbound, from the ledger only ----

;; #b0000031 is RETIRED — the pre-DENOMINATION_PLAN body, without (t, s). Do not
;; reuse; a stale sender must be rejected, not mis-parsed.
pay_era_bounty#b0000032
    query_id:uint64
    era_boundary:uint256
    beneficiary:MsgAddress
    t:Coins                 ;; ledger's POST-MINT T (nanoTON), DENOMINATION_PLAN P4
    s:Coins                 ;; ledger's POST-MINT S (nano-PRIMES)
  = InternalMsgBody;

;; D-99 §1.5. `kind` is 0 = REBATE_COMPOSITE_PER_POINT or 1 = REBATE_PRIME_FAMILY;
;; `points` is D(n) on kind 0 and ignored on kind 1. The vault's own genesis-fixed
;; rebateSchedule decides the TON value — the ledger decides eligibility and size
;; in points only, same D22 trust shape as pay_era_bounty. `n` is the idempotency key.
pay_special_number_rebate#b0000072
    query_id:uint64
    n:uint256
    kind:uint8
    points:uint16
    beneficiary:MsgAddress
    t:Coins
    s:Coins
  = InternalMsgBody;
;; sender MUST equal the ledger's fixed address (CONCEPT.md §3.4). Vault checks `era_boundary`
;; against its own genesis-fixed era-bounty schedule (params.json
;; genesis.era_bounty_schedule) and that this boundary has not already paid
;; (one-shot per boundary, dict keyed by era_boundary, cardinality <= number
;; of primorials ever reached — grows far slower than n, no ceiling concern:
;; even after 5,000 years of continuous mints the primorial sequence has
;; produced only a few dozen boundaries).
;;
;; THE SCHEDULE IS TON-DENOMINATED (DENOMINATION_PLAN P4, contract note D22).
;; Each entry is `(bounty_ton, max_primes)`; the vault pays
;;   amount = min(bounty_ton * s / t, max_primes)
;; i.e. the PRIMES that `bounty_ton` buys at the floor `p_f = T/S` this mint just
;; set. A fixed nominal PRIMES bounty would inflate with the floor (~45x over
;; year one at baseline demand); a TON-denominated one holds its designed value
;; and drains the vault more slowly as the floor rises.
;;
;; `t`/`s` come from the ledger because the vault cannot call a get-method, and
;; they are BOUNDED rather than trusted: `max_primes` is genesis-fixed and
;; address-determining, so a wrong snapshot can only under-pay, never drain.
;; Paid by TEP-74 `transfer` from the vault's own pre-funded jetton wallet, not
;; by `mint` — see the vault contract's D20.

;; ---- inbound, from an allow-listed v1.1 program contract ----

pay_program_bounty#90000002
    query_id:uint64
    program_tag:uint32     ;; identifies which allow-listed program (e.g. quests);
                            ;; must match the sender's entry, and rides in the
                            ;; payout's query_id so a bounce finds the track (V26.1)
    beneficiary:MsgAddress
    amount:Coins
  = InternalMsgBody;
;; sender MUST be present in the genesis-fixed allow-list dict (address ->
;; per-program remaining budget). Vault decrements that program's remaining
;; budget and sends a TEP-74 transfer for `amount`. Genesis allow-lists the
;; three vouchers, one entry per distinct program_tag. The allow-list itself cannot be
;; edited post-genesis by anything in v1 (no message type exists to do so);
;; adding a v1.1 program requires the same class of action as any other
;; protocol upgrade — a fresh contract deploy plus (if ever needed) a
;; venue-timelock-style, separately-decided governance path, explicitly out
;; of v1's scope.

;; `accrue_discovery#90000005`, `claim_discovery#90000006`, `credit_discovery#93000005`
;; and the vault's `floor_quote` arm are RETIRED by D-202 with the constellation
;; discovery bounty. Its PRIMES stay in the vault for §9.6's riddles.


;; D-53/B12.1, D-188. `pay_era_bounty`/`pay_special_number_rebate` mark the
;; flag paid and send the TEP-74 transfer with query_id =
;; `2^62 | kind<<61 | key` (kind 0 = era boundary, 1 = special n). A payout
;; that LANDS leaves no journal row. A genuine bounce is caught by the vault's
;; own `onBouncedMessage`, which clears the flag and writes the row from the
;; returned transfer (beneficiary, amount); a payout the balance guard defers
;; writes its row without sending.
;;
;; V26.1: `pay_program_bounty` is NEVER journalled. It sends with query_id =
;; `2^63 | 2^62 | program_tag`, and a bounce re-credits the tagged allow-list
;; track directly. There is no row of its for this message to replay (702). This message replays that row — same
;; beneficiary, same amount, decided once, never re-decided here — and deletes
;; it, so a second call fails closed with 702. The caller funds the hop:
;; >= 0.15 TON attached (`RETRY_PAYOUT_VALUE`, 103 below it).
retry_bounty_payout#90000004
    query_id:uint64
  = InternalMsgBody;

;; TEP-74's excess return, ACCEPTED AND KEPT. Not redefined here (the standard
;; jetton opcodes are reused verbatim, see jetton.tlb) — listed because this
;; contract RECEIVES it, which is a fact about its inbound surface and was for a
;; long time an untrue one.
;;
;; `payOut` names this vault as `response_destination` on every pushed route
;; (H11: `TRANSFER_GAS` comes out of the vault's own balance, so the change is
;; the vault's), and the recipient's jetton wallet answers each payout with
;; `excesses#d53276db`. Until 2026-09-17 the vault had no handler and the reply
;; aborted with exit 101 every time. Nothing was lost — the wallet sends it
;; non-bounceable, so the credit phase had already landed the TON — but the whole
;; MINT TRACE reads FAILED in an explorer when any transaction in it aborts
;; (testnet trace 8c354845...d724a). Permissionless by design: nothing moves.
excesses#d53276db
    query_id:uint64
  = InternalMsgBody;

;; The bounce-repair journal: 0 = paid_eras, 1 = special.paid_specials. Keyed
;; by the vault's own `journal_key` counter. A row exists only for an era or
;; special payout that was deferred or bounced (D-188 point 3); program payouts
;; are repaired onto their book and never journalled
;; (V26.1).
retry_entry$_
    kind:uint1
    key:uint256
    beneficiary:MsgAddress
    amount:Coins
  = RetryEntry;

;; ---- get-methods (§9.1) ----
;;
;; get_vault_config -> (ledger, jetton_master, jetton_wallet, wallet_set:int)
;;
;;
;; get_era_schedule(era_boundary:uint256) -> (scheduled:int, bounty_ton:Coins,
;;                                             max_primes:Coins, paid:int)
;;   §7 / §9.1 — the era ceremony's fixed VALUE and its nominal cap, so a reader
;;   can recompute the payout as `bounty_ton * S / T` from this call plus the
;;   ledger's `getRatchetState`, rather than being shown a printed constant.
;;
;; get_vault_payouts -> (paid_total:Coins, payout_count:uint32)
;;   §3.3 / §11.21 — the payout half of the circulating-supply report. A bounty
;;   payout moves tokens into circulation without touching `S`; a burn removes
;;   them without touching `S`; the two are reported as two dashboard numbers and
;;   never netted, because they are funded from opposite ends of the same
;;   accounting and netting them hides which one is doing the work.
;;   Counted at SEND, exactly like `paid_eras` is set at send, so the two agree
;;   with each other and a bounced transfer overstates both by the same amount —
;;   the pre-existing documented limitation of the bounce handler, not a new one.
;;   The vault's REMAINING balance is not here: it lives on the vault's own jetton
;;   wallet (get_wallet_data), and `vault size − paid ≈ balance` is the check that
;;   costs a reader nothing to run.
;;
;; get_vault_funded -> Coins
;;   V26.7 — the PRIMES genesis declared into the vault (address-determining
;;   deploy data, `genesis.bounty_vault_size_primes`). An era bounty or special
;;   rebate that `funded − paid_total` cannot cover is refused before any send:
;;   no flag, no journal row, no bounce. It reads unpaid and is forfeit.
;;
;; get_deferred_payouts -> (deferred_count:uint32, journal_key:uint64)
;;   H12 / DECISIONS.md D-129. A payout this contract OWES and has not delivered:
;;   either the balance guard deferred it (the vault could not afford the 0.1 TON
;;   jetton hop out of its own balance, so the row was journalled and nothing was
;;   sent) or its transfer bounced and the row was rolled back. Deliberately NOT a
;;   third field on get_vault_payouts: that pair is the §3.3 supply report, and a
;;   deferred payout is a liability, not supply.
;;   `journal_key` is the NEXT journal key the vault will issue. It bounds the
;;   key space so anyone can walk it: read get_retry_entry on 0 .. journal_key-1
;;   and fire retry_bounty_payout on a retryable row; a consumed or unwritten key
;;   fails closed with 702, so the scan cannot double-pay.
